# Secrets — never commit. This repo is a PUBLIC fork.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Dependencies
node_modules/

# Source corpus — the BIS standard PDFs, and these ARE tracked.
#
# This was ignored at first, on the grounds that the standards are not ours to
# redistribute. That is still true in general, and worth remembering before
# adding a sixth document: these five are committed deliberately so that a clone
# has a working corpus and working citation links the moment it starts, which is
# the whole point of the demo. Treat the folder as read-only reference material.
# Replace or regenerate in place rather than adding alongside.
#
# If you ever do need to strip the corpus from a copy, do it in a fork rather
# than here — a `git rm` leaves the blobs reachable in history anyway.

# Prepared index snapshots.
#
# The one bundle this repo ships IS tracked, so a clone starts from a working
# index instead of 5-20 minutes of CPU embedding. Everything else is ignored:
# a snapshot is a derived artefact, anyone can rebuild one with
# `npm run index:export`, and re-running that should never quietly stage another
# 19 MB. To add a second bundle on purpose, negate it here first.
index-snapshots/*
!index-snapshots/20260927T115319Z-ollama-nomic-embed-text-768d/
!index-snapshots/LATEST
!index-snapshots/README.md

# Local artifacts
*.log
.DS_Store
